Usage: recite say [flags] [TEXT...]

Text to verified audio file (default command)

Flags:
  -allow-unverified
    	exit 0 when a chunk stays unverified
  -chapters
    	write chapter markers from the headings (default on for m4a and m4b with headings)
  -chunk-seconds SECONDS
    	segmentation budget in SECONDS per chunk (default 25)
  -code MODE
    	Markdown code blocks: MODE skip, or announce (say "Code block omitted.") (default "skip")
  -date-style STYLE
    	spoken date STYLE: us, uk or iso (default "us")
  -dry-run
    	print the chunk plan and estimates (cache hits, audio, wall time, list price); no network, no login
  -effort EFFORT
    	reasoning EFFORT: minimal, low, medium, high, xhigh (default "minimal")
  -emotion PRESET
    	delivery PRESET: neutral, warm, calm, excited, serious, sad, whisper, newsreader, storyteller (default "neutral")
  -f PATH
    	read text from PATH
  -file PATH
    	read text from PATH
  -force
    	overwrite the output
  -format FMT
    	output FMT: wav pcm mp3 m4a m4b opus ogg flac (default from the extension, else wav)
  -gap-list DUR
    	gap after a list item, DUR or MIN..MAX (default "350ms..500ms")
  -gap-paragraph DUR
    	gap after a paragraph, DUR or MIN..MAX (default "550ms..800ms")
  -gap-section DUR
    	gap after a section, DUR or MIN..MAX (default "1.1s..1.5s")
  -gap-seed SEED
    	SEED of the random gaps; the same seed gives the same gaps
  -gap-sentence DUR
    	gap after a sentence, DUR or MIN..MAX (default "200ms..350ms")
  -guard POLICY
    	text guard POLICY: fix, strict, warn or off (default "fix")
  -input-format FORMAT
    	input FORMAT: text, markdown, or spoken (a prepare script: no guard, no spoken-form rules); default markdown for .md and .markdown files, else text
  -jobs N
    	render N chunks at once, 1 to 6 (default 3)
  -keep-rejected DIR
    	save every rejected take and its report in DIR
  -loudness PRESET
    	loudness PRESET: podcast, audiobook or none (default podcast for encoded formats, none for wav, pcm and -o -)
  -manifest PATH
    	write the manifest to PATH (default <output>.json)
  -marks
    	read inline speech marks such as {{spell|API}} (default on for spoken input)
  -max-attempts N
    	renders per chunk, N (default 3)
  -max-input BYTES
    	input size limit in BYTES (default 10485760)
  -model MODEL
    	speech MODEL: gpt-realtime-2.1, gpt-realtime-2, gpt-realtime-2.1-mini (default "gpt-realtime-2.1")
  -model-unchecked
    	accept any --model name
  -no-cache
    	neither read nor write the take cache
  -no-manifest
    	write no manifest
  -no-marks
    	read {{…}} as plain text
  -no-trim
    	keep the leading and trailing silence of each take
  -normalize MODE
    	spoken-form MODE: auto or off (default "auto")
  -normalize-disable RULE,…
    	turn off spoken-form rules, RULE,… (repeatable)
  -o PATH
    	write audio to PATH, or - for stdout (default <file stem>.<format> or speech-<timestamp>.<format>)
  -output PATH
    	write audio to PATH, or - for stdout (default <file stem>.<format> or speech-<timestamp>.<format>)
  -play
    	play the output when done
  -read-alt
    	read the alt text of Markdown images
  -refresh
    	render every chunk anew; the takes still go to the cache
  -request-extra-attempts N
    	extra renders for a request-like chunk, N (default 1)
  -retry-effort LIST
    	LIST of efforts for attempts 1, 2, 3…, the last repeating, e.g. minimal,low,medium (default off)
  -sample-rate HZ
    	output sample rate HZ: 16000, 22050, 24000, 44100, 48000 (default "24000")
  -session-chunks N
    	renders per speech session before it is replaced, N (default 50)
  -speed SPEED
    	SPEED from 0.25 to 1.5 in steps of 0.01 (default "1.0")
  -split-sections
    	write one file per heading, NN-<slug>.<format>, into the -o directory
  -strict-output
    	write no output when a chunk stays unverified
  -style TEXT
    	free-text delivery TEXT, sent after the rules as "Delivery:"
  -subtitles FMT
    	write subtitles FMT (srt or vtt) next to the output
  -verify MODE
    	verification MODE: strict, normal or off (default "normal")
  -verify-jobs N
    	verify N takes at once (default 2 × --jobs)
  -voice VOICE
    	VOICE: alloy, ash, ballad, coral, echo, sage, shimmer, verse, marin, cedar (default "cedar")

Global flags:
  -auth-source SOURCE
    	auth SOURCE: auto, codex or file (default auto)
  -codex-bin PATH
    	codex binary PATH
  -codex-home DIR
    	codex home DIR
  -config PATH
    	read config from PATH
  -debug-dir DIR
    	write debug artifacts to DIR
  -json
    	machine-readable output
  -log-file PATH
    	write the log to PATH
  -no-color
    	disable colour
  -profile NAME
    	use config profile NAME
  -q	quiet: errors only
  -quiet
    	quiet: errors only
  -v	verbose (repeatable)
  -verbose
    	verbose (repeatable)
